      "summary": "The Unix worker uses the filesystem root instead of a fresh temporary working directory. The environment test also does not verify what the child actually inherits, so it can pass when environment clearing is removed.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 219,
          "message": "On Unix, the worker does not get a fresh temporary working directory that is deleted after the run.",
          "confidence": 0.96,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "On non-Windows platforms, Parse calls ChooseWorkingDirectory, which returns \"/\". Its finally block deletes a directory only on Windows.",
            "failureScenario": "On Linux, every worker starts with the filesystem root as its working directory; no fresh temporary directory is created or deleted. This fails the acceptance criterion and lets relative file operations run from the root directory."
          }
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/IsolatedPdfParserTests.cs",
          "line": 347,
          "message": "The empty-environment test does not detect removal of Environment.Clear(), as required by AC-4 and AC-5.",
          "confidence": 0.96,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The test checks that startInfo.Environment is empty, but ProcessStartInfo can inherit the parent environment when its environment collection is empty. The test does not start a child to inspect its actual environment.",
            "failureScenario": "If Environment.Clear() is removed from CreateStartInfo, this assertion can still pass while the child inherits the API process environment. The required regression test therefore does not fail when the empty-environment behavior is broken."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
