      },
      "summary": "The tests cover several parser and supervision scenarios, but the Unix worker directory does not meet AC-4, and the environment assertion cannot catch removal of the clearing behavior.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 163,
          "message": "AC-4 requires a fresh, empty temporary working directory that is deleted after the run. The Unix path uses \"/\" and has no per-run directory to delete.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "ChooseWorkingDirectory returns \"/\" on Unix, and Parse only creates and deletes a per-run directory on Windows.",
            "failureScenario": "On Linux, the worker starts in the filesystem root instead of a fresh, empty temporary directory, and Parse does not delete a per-run working directory. The explicit AC-4 launch behavior is unmet."
          }
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/IsolatedPdfParserTests.cs",
          "line": 347,
          "message": "The empty-environment assertion does not verify that the child will receive an empty environment; it passes even if the environment-clearing call is removed.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The test asserts that ProcessStartInfo.Environment is empty. That collection is empty by default, even when the child will inherit the parent environment; it does not verify that CreateStartInfo clears inherited variables.",
            "failureScenario": "If Environment.Clear() is removed, the assertion still passes while the launched worker inherits the API process environment. The named test therefore does not fail when the empty-environment behavior is removed, contrary to AC-4 and AC-5."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
